{"parentUuid":"ef8d3e6a-abf5-4c21-ac7a-aca743cd97a7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cfe22842-ba08-4ec5-a7d1-14fbd50c5f8f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017oNT8ETyR8vza2VMa41gGE","type":"tool_result","content":"270\t\n271\tRecovery:\n272\t  local old-current work is merged into /full/0000000000007\n273\t  local /full/current is replaced with remote fresh /full/current\n274\t```\n275\t\n276\tFinal remote state:\n277\t\n278\t```text\n279\t/full/0000000000007 has IDs 1..105\n280\t/full/current remains fresh\n281\t```\n282\t\n283\tGeneration 7 can exceed the nominal threshold. That is acceptable. The more\n284\timportant property is that each raw transcript is reachable from one generation,\n285\tnot duplicated across the archive and current generation.\n286\t\n287\t## Archived Ref Collisions\n288\t\n289\tArchived generation refs are treated as effectively immutable cleanup units. If\n290\tpre-push tries to publish a pending archive ref and the remote already has that\n291\tsame archive name at a different commit, the push surfaces an error instead of\n292\tsilently merging or renaming the local archive.\n293\t\n294\tAutomatic recovery here is intentionally conservative:\n295\t\n296\t- Merging two archives could hide corruption or stale local state.\n297\t- Merging could also make a generation much larger than the rotation threshold.\n298\t- Renaming the local archive to the next number adds complexity and may not\n299\t  preserve the intended generation boundary.\n300\t- Overwriting the remote archive is not acceptable.\n301\t\n302\tThe expected common case is handled by remote rotation conflict recovery on\n303\t`/full/current`. A direct archive-name collision should be investigated from\n304\tthe concrete error and logs.\n305\t\n306\t## Cleanup and GC\n307\t\n308\tCleanup operates only on archived `/full/<N>` refs:\n309\t\n310\t1. List archived generation refs.\n311\t2. Read each archive's `generation.json`.\n312\t3. If the newest checkpoint in the archive is older than the retention window,\n313\t   delete the whole ref on the checkpoint remote.\n314\t4. Git GC can reclaim the raw transcript blobs once no refs reach them.\n315\t\n316\t`/main` is never cleaned up this way. It contains the permanent, compact data\n317\tneeded for checkpoint listing, explain, and API reads.\n318\t\n319\tThe rotation and recovery rules above are designed to preserve one cleanup\n320\tproperty: deleting an archived generation should make that generation's raw\n321\ttranscript blobs unreachable unless they are also intentionally preserved\n322\telsewhere.\n323\t\n324\t## Failure Windows\n325\t\n326\tLocal rotation is deliberately ordered so the pre-push handoff exists before the\n327\tvisible generation reset:\n328\t\n329\t- If the pending marker cannot be written, rotation aborts before moving refs.\n330\t- If a ref update fails after the marker is written, the marker is removed\n331\t  best-effort.\n332\t- If the process stops after `/full/current` is reset, the pending marker\n333\t  remains and pre-push can publish the intended rotation.\n334\t- If a stale marker remains from an interrupted attempt where `/full/current`\n335\t  was never reset, including a stop after only the local archive ref moved,\n336\t  pre-push drops that stale reset publication before pushing pending archive\n337\t  refs. The raw transcript data is still reachable from local `/full/current`,\n338\t  so this does not lose checkpoint data.\n339\t\n340\tThese rules avoid the production failure mode where remote old\n341\t`/full/current` was merged back into a fresh local generation after rotation.\n342\t"}]},"uuid":"5476113c-1611-4521-b52a-4da95953737f","timestamp":"2026-05-11T21:16:12.394Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/fix/checkpoints-v2-rotation-logic/docs/architecture/checkpoints-v2-rotation.md","content":"\nRecovery:\n  local old-current work is merged into /full/0000000000007\n  local /full/current is replaced with remote fresh /full/current\n```\n\nFinal remote state:\n\n```text\n/full/0000000000007 has IDs 1..105\n/full/current remains fresh\n```\n\nGeneration 7 can exceed the nominal threshold. That is acceptable. The more\nimportant property is that each raw transcript is reachable from one generation,\nnot duplicated across the archive and current generation.\n\n## Archived Ref Collisions\n\nArchived generation refs are treated as effectively immutable cleanup units. If\npre-push tries to publish a pending archive ref and the remote already has that\nsame archive name at a different commit, the push surfaces an error instead of\nsilently merging or renaming the local archive.\n\nAutomatic recovery here is intentionally conservative:\n\n- Merging two archives could hide corruption or stale local state.\n- Merging could also make a generation much larger than the rotation threshold.\n- Renaming the local archive to the next number adds complexity and may not\n  preserve the intended generation boundary.\n- Overwriting the remote archive is not acceptable.\n\nThe expected common case is handled by remote rotation conflict recovery on\n`/full/current`. A direct archive-name collision should be investigated from\nthe concrete error and logs.\n\n## Cleanup and GC\n\nCleanup operates only on archived `/full/<N>` refs:\n\n1. List archived generation refs.\n2. Read each archive's `generation.json`.\n3. If the newest checkpoint in the archive is older than the retention window,\n   delete the whole ref on the checkpoint remote.\n4. Git GC can reclaim the raw transcript blobs once no refs reach them.\n\n`/main` is never cleaned up this way. It contains the permanent, compact data\nneeded for checkpoint listing, explain, and API reads.\n\nThe rotation and recovery rules above are designed to preserve one cleanup\nproperty: deleting an archived generation should make that generation's raw\ntranscript blobs unreachable unless they are also intentionally preserved\nelsewhere.\n\n## Failure Windows\n\nLocal rotation is deliberately ordered so the pre-push handoff exists before the\nvisible generation reset:\n\n- If the pending marker cannot be written, rotation aborts before moving refs.\n- If a ref update fails after the marker is written, the marker is removed\n  best-effort.\n- If the process stops after `/full/current` is reset, the pending marker\n  remains and pre-push can publish the intended rotation.\n- If a stale marker remains from an interrupted attempt where `/full/current`\n  was never reset, including a stop after only the local archive ref moved,\n  pre-push drops that stale reset publication before pushing pending archive\n  refs. The raw transcript data is still reachable from local `/full/current`,\n  so this does not lose checkpoint data.\n\nThese rules avoid the production failure mode where remote old\n`/full/current` was merged back into a fresh local generation after rotation.\n","numLines":73,"startLine":270,"totalLines":342}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ef8d3e6a-abf5-4c21-ac7a-aca743cd97a7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/fix/checkpoints-v2-rotation-logic","sessionId":"e5e1da62-a043-4254-81ed-73be6ad15b8c","version":"2.1.126","gitBranch":"fix/checkpoints-v2-rotation-logic-docs"}
